# Generated into rpmbuild/SPECS/bpfc.spec by `make rpm`; @VERSION@/@RELEASE@ come from the Makefile.

# Fallbacks so the spec also builds where systemd-rpm-macros is unavailable.
%{!?_unitdir: %global _unitdir /usr/lib/systemd/system}

# rpmbuild --with static: statically linked binaries that run in any image,
# whatever its libc (used for builds made outside RHEL).
%bcond_with static

Name:           bpfc
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        @RELEASE@%{?dist}
Summary:        eBPF compiler for TC packet programs, with a daemon to keep them attached

License:        GPL-3.0-or-later
URL:            https://github.com/briantmiller/bpfc
Source0:        %{name}-%{version}.tar.gz

BuildRequires:  gcc
BuildRequires:  make
BuildRequires:  kernel-headers
BuildRequires:  systemd-rpm-macros
%if %{with static}
BuildRequires:  glibc-static
%endif
# Ordering only, not a dependency: the package installs and runs without
# systemd (containers); the unit file is simply unused there.
%{?systemd_ordering}

%description
bpfc compiles a small packet matching and rewriting language straight to
eBPF bytecode (no LLVM/Clang) and attaches it to a network interface's TC
ingress or egress hook.

bpfcd keeps the programs in /etc/bpfc/interfaces.d attached: it installs
them at boot and when interfaces appear, applies changes on reload with an
atomic replace, and reinstalls or reports programs removed by other tools.
bpfcctl shows what is installed and from which file.

%package container
Summary:        Entrypoint for running bpfcd in a container without systemd
BuildArch:      noarch
Requires:       %{name} = %{version}-%{release}

%description container
bpfcd-entrypoint starts bpfcd as a container's main process (PID 1), with
no systemd. It checks the container's capabilities, prepares bpffs for
pinned maps and execs bpfcd in the foreground. Includes an example
Containerfile and run instructions.

%package scripts
Summary:        Program generators for bpfc: the FEC/ARQ dataplane, with profiles and examples
BuildArch:      noarch
Requires:       %{name} = %{version}-%{release}
Requires:       bash
Requires:       coreutils
Requires:       gawk

%description scripts
bpfc-dataplane-gen generates an FEC/ARQ dataplane (forward error
correction, retransmission, loss and capacity measurement) for a link as
bpfc programs that bpfcd installs, over Layer 2 or UDP, from built-in or
local profiles. bpfc-dataplane-status shows its state and changes its
runtime settings. Includes the built-in profiles, the design notes and
example programs.

%prep
%autosetup

%build
%make_build VERSION=%{version} CFLAGS="%{optflags}" LDFLAGS="%{?build_ldflags}" \
    STATIC=%{?with_static:1}%{!?with_static:0}

%install
%make_install VERSION=%{version} \
    PREFIX=%{_prefix} SBINDIR=%{_sbindir} MANDIR=%{_mandir} DATADIR=%{_datadir} \
    DOCDIR=%{_docdir}/%{name} CONTAINER_DOCDIR=%{_docdir}/%{name}-container \
    SCRIPTS_DOCDIR=%{_docdir}/%{name}-scripts \
    UNITDIR=%{_unitdir} SYSCONFDIR=%{_sysconfdir}

%post
%{?systemd_post:%systemd_post bpfcd.service}

%preun
%{?systemd_preun:%systemd_preun bpfcd.service}

%postun
# Restart on upgrade: running programs are adopted, not reinstalled.
%{?systemd_postun_with_restart:%systemd_postun_with_restart bpfcd.service}

%files
%license LICENSE
%{_docdir}/%{name}/
%{_sbindir}/bpfc
%{_sbindir}/bpfcd
%{_sbindir}/bpfcctl
%{_mandir}/man8/bpfc.8*
%{_mandir}/man8/bpfcd.8*
%{_mandir}/man8/bpfcctl.8*
%{_mandir}/man5/bpfc.conf.5*
%{_unitdir}/bpfcd.service
%dir %{_sysconfdir}/bpfc
%config(noreplace) %{_sysconfdir}/bpfc/bpfc.conf
%dir %{_sysconfdir}/bpfc/interfaces.d
%dir %{_sysconfdir}/bpfc/include

%files container
%{_sbindir}/bpfcd-entrypoint
%{_docdir}/%{name}-container/

%files scripts
%{_sbindir}/bpfc-dataplane-gen
%{_sbindir}/bpfc-dataplane-status
%dir %{_sysconfdir}/bpfc/dataplane
%dir %{_sysconfdir}/bpfc/dataplane/profiles.d
%{_datadir}/bpfc/
%{_docdir}/%{name}-scripts/

%changelog
* Wed Nov 04 2026 bpfc maintainers <brun064@gmail.com> - 0.1.1-4
- New bpfc-scripts subpackage (noarch, optional): the FEC/ARQ dataplane
  generator and status tool (bpfc-dataplane-gen, bpfc-dataplane-status) in
  /usr/sbin, the built-in profiles (direct, wan, geo, leo) in
  /usr/share/bpfc/dataplane/profiles, /etc/bpfc/dataplane/profiles.d for
  local profiles, and DESIGN.md and example programs in
  /usr/share/doc/bpfc-scripts
- bpfc-dataplane-gen: UDP carriers (carrier udp: outer IPv4/UDP to the
  peer, with peer learning behind NAT and keepalives; carrier udp-inline:
  UDP after the original IP header, TOS and addresses kept for QoS on a
  private routed WAN), protect
  prefixes, path-mtu
- bpfc: remove-l2 (the counterpart of insert-l2; skb->protocol unchanged)

* Thu Oct 29 2026 bpfc maintainers <brun064@gmail.com> - 0.1.1-3
- bpfc del-bytes: the default (buffered) path zero-filled the packet after
  the offset whenever the offset was above 0; it now copies only the tail
- bpfc del-bytes: a packet shorter than offset+length is left unchanged
  (the unrolled path used to cut the tail, deleting bytes before the offset)
- bpfc del-bytes: no longer overwrites the set-reg-loop counter (R7)
- bpfc del-bytes: drops the packet if the kernel refuses the new length
  instead of passing on shifted bytes at the old length
- bpfc: more than 16 variables is an error instead of a crash

* Thu Oct 29 2026 bpfc maintainers <brun064@gmail.com> - 0.1.1-2
- Add bpfc-container subpackage with bpfcd-entrypoint for systemd-free containers
- Drop the hard dependency on systemd (ordering only)
- bpfcd: BPFCD_* environment overrides, reaps orphans as PID 1, blocks
  stop signals from the first instruction
- bpfcctl: correct daemon status when run as a non-root user
- Optional static build (rpmbuild --with static)

* Wed Oct 28 2026 bpfc maintainers <brun064@gmail.com> - 0.1.0-1
- Add bpfcd daemon, bpfcctl status tool and systemd unit
- bpfc: atomic replace, per-priority delete (-D), program naming (-n),
  id/tag reporting (-I), netlink error checking, comment handling in -f files
